{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift automatically imports simple, constant-like macros, declared with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#define"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directive, as global constants. Macros are imported when they use literals for string,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"floating-point, or integer values, or use operators like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":">"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between literals or previously defined macros. This example defines some simple macros"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in a C header:"}]},{"syntax":"occ","type":"codeListing","code":["#define FADE_ANIMATION_DURATION 0.35","#define VERSION_STRING \"2.2.10.0a\"","#define MAX_RESOLUTION 1268","","#define HALF_RESOLUTION (MAX_RESOLUTION \/ 2)","#define IS_HIGH_RES (MAX_RESOLUTION > 1024)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When imported into Swift, the macros in the above example are equivalent to these"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"constant declarations:"}]},{"code":["let FADE_ANIMATION_DURATION = 0.35","let VERSION_STRING = \"2.2.10.0a\"","let MAX_RESOLUTION = 1268","","let HALF_RESOLUTION = 634","let IS_HIGH_RES = true"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Use Functions and Generics Instead of Complex Macros","level":3,"anchor":"Use-Functions-and-Generics-Instead-of-Complex-Macros","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"C macros that are more complex than simple constant definitions have no counterpart","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in Swift. You use complex macros in C and Objective-C to avoid type-checking constraints","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or to avoid retyping large amounts of boilerplate code. However, macros can make","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"debugging and refactoring difficult. In Swift, you can use functions and generics","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to achieve the same results without any compromises.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"role":"article","title":"Using Imported C Macros in Swift"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-macros-in-swift","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use imported C-defined macros as constants."}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Language Interoperability with C and C++","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Language-Interoperability-with-C-and-C++"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Swift","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Build apps using a powerful open language.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift","abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to call imported functions that are declared in a C header.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Using Imported C Functions in Swift","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-functions-in-swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift":{"type":"topic","title":"Customizing Your C Code for Swift","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift","role":"article","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CF_SWIFT_NAME"},{"type":"text","text":" macro to group functions that have related behavior."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swift\/customizing-your-c-code-for-swift"},"doc://com.apple.Swift/documentation/Swift/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","title":"Using Imported C Structs and Unions in Swift","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swift\/using-imported-c-structs-and-unions-in-swift","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how Swift represents imported C structures and unions, including types with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bitfields and unnamed fields."}]},"Swift-PageImage-card.png":{"variants":[{"traits":["2x","light"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card@2x.png"},{"traits":["2x","dark"],"url":"\/images\/com.apple.Swift\/Swift-PageImage-card~dark@2x.png"}],"identifier":"Swift-PageImage-card.png","alt":"An orange Swift logo on a gradient background.","type":"image"}}}